  "solution": {
    "brief": "Wasp example 14: continuing into advanced topics",
    "principle": "\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Tutorial 15 (wasp_15) is the direct successor to tutorial 14 — it continues the advanced topics progression, further deepening modular assembly and rules-based aggregation techniques. Tutorial 14 is the direct prerequisite for understanding the advanced topics explored in tutorial 15.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: The advanced topics series that begins at tutorial 14 extends well beyond tutorial 15, progressing into a dedicated constraints sub-series that includes tutorials 28 and 29 (wasp_29), which covers constraint-based stochastic aggregation with adjacency and connection-configuration rules. Tutorial 14 is an indirect foundational prerequisite for this extended constraints progression.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: The advanced topics series that begins at tutorial 14 extends further still into the constraints sub-series, now confirmed to progress through tutorial 31 (wasp_31), which continues constraint-based aggregation with plane-constraint techniques. Tutorial 14 is an indirect foundational prerequisite for this extended constraints progression (wasp_28 → wasp_29 → wasp_30 → wasp_31).\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: The constraints sub-series now confirmed to extend through tutorial 32 (wasp_32), which continues constraint-based aggregation with mesh-constraint techniques. Tutorial 14 is an indirect foundational prerequisite for this extended constraints progression (wasp_28 → wasp_29 → wasp_30 → wasp_31 → wasp_32).\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: The foundational multi-part, rule-based aggregation techniques established in wasp_14 are extended in more advanced patterns (such as wasp_stochastic_aggregation_smart_attributes) through smart attributes and mesh-based part geometry — demonstrating that the connection and rule infrastructure introduced here scales to attribute-driven, stochastic workflows.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: The multi-part, rule-based aggregation infrastructure established in wasp_14 scales to advanced workflows (such as wasp_stochastic_aggregation_hierarchy) that introduce part hierarchy retrieval — enabling aggregation systems to organize and query parts by hierarchical relationships alongside connection-direction and rule-generation logic. Part hierarchy is an advanced structural concept built on the multi-part foundations here.",
